  "slug": "automated-microscopy-2e31",
  "summary": "New methods target attribution errors in spatial transcriptomics and multiplexed imaging: transcripts to cells, pixels to markers, spots to cell types.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is correcting how measurements are attributed to cells and cell types in spatial data. Optimal transport recurs. Tracel reassigns transcripts or bin counts to cells against matched scRNA-seq references. spOT-NMF performs reference-free deconvolution with proximity-aware niche mapping. SPECHTacle combines Waddington OT with Shannon entropy to flag preferentially altered populations. Deconvolution is also being refined: SWIMR integrates multiple reference panels with spatial correlation, and ARCADE separates cell-type abundance from continuous intratype transcriptional state. Downstream statistics are becoming confound-aware. SpatioCAD's density-aware graph diffusion reduces false-positive spatially variable genes, TileScope quantifies relationships beyond colocalization, and CRISP characterizes cross-signal interactions. Parallel imaging work applies the same logic. PixAQ replaces shared segmentation masks with marker-specific pixel attribution in imaging mass cytometry, and CardioShift models nested variance in single-cell cardiomyocyte function. DynaCell and MaCADEMIA supply evaluation and quantification infrastructure. VIGAT and MAD nucleus editing are adjacent outliers.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
